  "role": "Assault skirmisher",
  "summary": "A fast assault skirmisher behind a seamless shell. Four cycling emitters track well inside two hundred metres, then heat and distance take their price.",
  "lore": "Pallvaults were stored standing directly on their depot floors, their broad upper housings nearly touching the roof. Compact manuals assumed service docks able to exchange whole assemblies. Tessellan workshops developed slower methods using jigs, careful measurements and heavy recovery crews. Repairs are possible, costly and dependent on finding the right components. An intact Pallvault moves more quickly than its broad silhouette suggests. Its standard emitter banks make a short exchange formidable; repeated volleys still demand restraint.",
